# BrainBox — environment
#
# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; this file is not, so never put
# a real value in here.
#
# Nothing here is injected for you. Five values are required; the two Redis
# ones are optional, and rooms fall back to Postgres without them. So is the
# Ably key, and moves fall back to polling without it.


# --------------------------------------------------------------------- app ---
# Absolute URL of this deployment. Used to build shareable room links, which
# have to be absolute to be worth sharing, and read in the browser.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL="http://localhost:3000"


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- database ---
# Neon Postgres, pooled (-pooler in the host). Every request the app serves
# goes through this one. Serverless opens a lot of short connections, and the
# pooler is what stops Neon running out of them. Keep ?sslmode=require.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@ep-example-123456-pooler.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech/brainbox?sslmode=require"

# Optional, and only for migrations. The pooler runs in transaction mode and
# cannot hold the session a schema change needs, so `drizzle-kit migrate` wants
# the direct URL — the same string without `-pooler`. It is never read at
# runtime, so Vercel does not need it: set it locally and leave it unset there.
# If it is missing, migrations fall back to DATABASE_URL and may fail on DDL.
DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED="postgresql://user:password@ep-example-123456.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech/brainbox?sslmode=require"


# -------------------------------------------------------------------- auth ---
# Better Auth. Email and password — no OAuth provider, so there is nothing to
# register with GitHub or Google and no client id or secret to carry.
#
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET signs and encrypts sessions. Generate one per environment;
# local and production must NOT share it. Changing it logs everyone out.
#
#   openssl rand -base64 32
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET="generate-me-do-not-copy-this-value"

# The base URL Better Auth serves its routes from. Unlike some libraries this
# is not inferred — set it explicitly, and set it to the deployed URL in
# production or sign-in callbacks resolve against the wrong host.
BETTER_AUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"


# ------------------------------------------------------------------- rooms ---
# Optional. Online rooms prefer Redis and fall back to Postgres on their own —
# see lib/rooms-store.js — so leaving these unset is a supported way to run,
# not a broken one. Both must be set for Redis to be used at all.
#
# The REST pair, not the redis:// URL: the REST client works from serverless
# without holding a socket open. Upstash console > your database > REST API.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=""
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=""


# -------------------------------------------------------------------- live ---
# Optional. Without it the board polls, exactly as it does today: a move shows
# up on the other screen somewhere between 1.2 and 8 seconds later, depending
# on how long the room has been quiet. With it, the server publishes a nudge
# the moment a room changes and the other browser asks at once — call it a
# tenth of a second, and far fewer reads, because nothing is fetched while
# nothing is happening.
#
# Ably and not a socket of our own because a serverless function cannot hold a
# connection open for a whole game. Ably holds it; we only publish.
#
# ONE key, and it is a server secret. The browser never sees it: it asks
# /api/ably/token and gets a short-lived token scoped to the one room it is in.
# Do NOT give this a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix — see the note at the bottom of this
# file about what that prefix means.
#
# Ably dashboard > your app > API keys. The root key works; a dedicated key
# needs Publish and Subscribe on `room:*`. The format is appId.keyId:secret.
ABLY_API_KEY=""


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# On Vercel
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Add all of these, to Production / Preview / Development:
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL         https://<your-project>.vercel.app
#   DATABASE_URL                the POOLED Neon URL
#   BETTER_AUTH_SECRET          a DIFFERENT value from your local one
#   BETTER_AUTH_URL             https://<your-project>.vercel.app
#   UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL      production only, if you want rooms on Redis
#   UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN    production only
#   ABLY_API_KEY                if you want moves pushed instead of polled
#
# Leave DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED unset there — migrations are not run from a
# deployment.
#
# BETTER_AUTH_URL is a single fixed host, so preview deployments authenticate
# against the production URL rather than their own. That is fine for previews
# you only look at. If you ever need to sign in on a preview, set it per
# environment to https://$VERCEL_URL instead.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ is a publishing keyword: anything with that prefix is compiled
# into the browser bundle and is readable by anyone. Only NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL
# belongs there. If a key is ever given that prefix, treat that key as leaked.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rooms
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Rooms used to sit in a globalThis Map, which works under one node process and
# cannot work on Vercel: a player typing the code may land on an instance that
# has never seen the room. They now live in Redis when it is configured and
# answering, and in Postgres otherwise. The choice is made once, on first use,
# and a Redis that dies mid-game drops through to Postgres rather than taking
# the game with it.
#
# Whichever is holding them, the client polls with the version it already has
# and an unchanged room answers 304 — no board, no body, nothing to re-render.
# The hook backs that off from 1.2s to 8s while nothing happens, snaps back the
# moment something does, and stops entirely while the tab is hidden. That last
# one matters on Postgres: Neon bills compute time and scales to zero when idle,
# so an abandoned tab polling forever is what would keep it awake all night.
